# Normalise text in the repository, and pin LF for anything executed inside a
# Linux container. A shell script committed with CRLF from a Windows checkout
# fails in Alpine with a bare "\r: not found" - the file looks perfect in an
# editor and the container refuses to run it. The backup service mounts
# deploy/*.sh directly, so this is not hypothetical.
* text=auto

*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
deploy/Caddyfile* text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.db  binary
*.dump binary
*.xlsx binary
